  "tagline": "Vercel's globally replicated read-optimized config store (renamed Global Config in 2026).",
  "description": "Edge Config is a small, globally replicated key-value store on Vercel designed for data that is read on almost every request and written rarely: feature flags, A/B test buckets, redirects, IP blocklists. Reads typically finish in about a millisecond from any region because the data is pushed to Vercel's compute locations. In July 2026 Vercel renamed it Global Config, shipped @vercel/global-config as a drop-in SDK and raised store size to 1 MB on every plan; existing EDGE_CONFIG projects keep working. Write limits (about 100 per hour on paid plans) make it unsuitable for anything transactional.",
